      "problem": "On a field trip to a theme park, $150$ students out of $500$ rode a roller coaster. What percentage of students rode a roller coaster?",
      "worked_solution": "We're given a part and a whole, and we must find a percentage. So, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=\\text{part}÷\\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, \n\n- the part is the number of students who rode a roller coaster, which is $150,$ and\n\n- the whole is the total number of students, which is $500.$\n\nSubstituting our numbers into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=150÷500=\\frac{150}{500}.\n$$\n\nTo write this as a percentage, we create an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{150}{500}=\\frac{150÷5}{500÷5}=\\frac{30}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{100}=30%\n$$\n\nTherefore, $30%$ of the students rode a roller coaster.",
